      "problem": "What number can be added to $-35$ to get a sum of $0?$",
      "worked_solution": "The number that can be added to $-35$ to give $0$ is the additive inverse of $-35.$\n\nTo find the additive inverse of the number $-35$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain\n\n$$\n-\\,(-35)=35.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-35)+35=-35+35=0\\,✓\n$$",
